      <Text>SEQUENCE: CODA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="0" Page="0" Title="Epilogue"/>
      <Text>EXT. EPILOGUE - DAWN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Characters: ADA]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="0" Page="0" Title="Teaser" Synopsis="Cold open."/>
      <Text>INT. TEASER - MORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Conflict: Nobody will meet her eye.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="General">
      <Text>LOOSE NOTES</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Character: Ada — Pronouns: she/her · Role: Protagonist · Occupation: Ferry pilot · Age: 34 · Character Summary: Came home to sell the boat and stayed.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Never says what she means the first time.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Character: Cy — Role: Minor]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Library only, never placed.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Location: Kitchen — Type: Interior · Time Period: 1970s · Mood / Atmosphere: close, airless · Setting Description: Low ceiling, one window over the sink.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Shoot it smaller than it is.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Location: Barn — Type: Exterior]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Prop: Lantern — Story Function: Practical · Description: Brass, dented, still works.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Ada&apos;s father&apos;s.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Prop: Knife — Story Function: MacGuffin]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Theme: Grief — Statement: Grief unspoken hardens into blame. · Expression: Doors left open, meals left uneaten. · Opposition: Silence is also a kind of mercy.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Keep it out of the dialogue.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Theme: Hope — Expression: Light through water.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Arc: Ada thaws — Subject: Ada · Axis: guarded → open · Direction: Positive]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Three stages at most.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Arc: The town forgets — Subject: The town itself · Axis: memory → rumour]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Thought: Title idea]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>[Call it &quot;Low Water&quot;.]</Text>
    </Paragraph>
